            description: "Pollination: Requirements vary. Some cultivars are self-fruitful. Others require a pollinator.a. Disease notes: Summer rots are the most serious disease problems and can destroy an entire crop. No cultivars are resistant. Some cultivars are resistant to apple scab, powdery mildew, cedar apple rust or fire blight. These include Redfree, Prima, Priscilla, Jonafree, and Liberty (which performs poorly in North Carolina). Other considerations: In warmer regions, red cultivars may not color well"
